---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import { MotionRecipeToastsReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-recipe-toasts.tsx';
import { MotionRecipeToastsAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-recipe-toasts.ts';
import MotionRecipeToastsSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-recipe-toasts.svelte';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="recipes/toasts"
  title="Motion: toasts recipe"
  description="A toast queue whose messages enter one after the other, leave after six seconds or when dismissed, and let the others close the gap, in HTML, React, Angular and Svelte."
>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-recipe-toasts" previewHeight={[280, 256]}>
    <MotionRecipeToastsReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionRecipeToastsAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionRecipeToastsSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>
  <p>
    For a single message, use the Udixio <a href="/components/snackbar/overview">Snackbar</a>: it already enters and leaves
    on <code>@udixio/motion</code>. It has no queue, so build one as above when messages can pile up.
  </p>
  <h2>Why it is accessible</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The list is a polite live region (<code>aria-live="polite"</code>), rendered from the start: each toast added to it is read once, without taking focus.</li>
    <li>Each toast has a Dismiss button. A toast never holds the only way to do something: an Undo must also exist in the page.</li>
    <li>Six seconds leaves time to read a short message. For a longer one, raise the lifetime, or keep the toast until it is dismissed.</li>
    <li>Under reduced motion, the entry and the exit become a short fade, and the others take their new place at once.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Motion and timing</h2>
  <p>
    Each toast names two motions. <code>toast</code>, defined in the example, rises 16 px and grows from 96 % as it fades in;
    its exit is <code>out-of-flow</code>, so the toast leaves the flow when its exit starts and the others move up at once
    (the list is <code>relative</code> for that). <code>reflow</code> makes the others glide to their new place. The entry
    runs on <code>spring.default.spatial</code> and <code>spring.default.effects</code>, the exit on
    <code>spring.default.effects</code>, and the glide on <code>spring.default.spatial</code>. See
    <a href="/motion/lists">Lists</a>.
  </p>
</MotionPage>
